NNAAMMEE
       filefrag - report on file fragmentation

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ffiilleeffrraagg [ --bb_b_l_o_c_k_s_i_z_e ] [ --BBeeEEkkPPssvvVVxxXX ] [ _f_i_l_e_s_._._.  ]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ffiilleeffrraagg  reports  on  how badly fragmented a particular file might be.
       It makes allowances for indirect blocks for ext2 and ext3 file systems,
       but can be used on files for any file system.

       The  ffiilleeffrraagg  program initially attempts to get the extent information
       using FIEMAP ioctl which is more efficient and faster.   If  FIEMAP  is
       not supported then filefrag will fall back to using FIBMAP.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --BB     Force  the  use  of the older FIBMAP ioctl instead of the FIEMAP
              ioctl for testing purposes.

       --bb_b_l_o_c_k_s_i_z_e
              Use _b_l_o_c_k_s_i_z_e in bytes, or with [KMG] suffix, up to 1GB for out‐
              put  instead  of  the  file system blocksize.  For compatibility
              with earlier versions of ffiilleeffrraagg, if _b_l_o_c_k_s_i_z_e  is  unspecified
              it defaults to 1024 bytes.  Since _b_l_o_c_k_s_i_z_e is an optional argu‐
              ment, it must be added without any space after --bb.

       --ee     Print output in extent format, even for block-mapped files.

       --EE     Display the contents of ext4's extent status cache.   This  fea‐
              ture  is  not supported on all kernels, and is only supported on
              ext4 file systems.

       --kk     Use 1024-byte blocksize for output (identical to '-b1024').

       --PP     Pre-load the ext4 extent status cache for the file.  This is not
              supported  on  all  kernels,  and is only supported on ext4 file
              systems.

       --ss     Sync the file before requesting the mapping.

       --vv     Be verbose when checking for file fragmentation.

       --VV     Print version number of program and library.   If  given  twice,
              also  print  the FIEMAP flags that are understood by the current
              version.

       --xx     Display mapping of extended attributes.

       --XX     Display extent block numbers in hexadecimal format.

